    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-5665-9281"
abstract: >-
  An open specification proposing that a generation of AI be defined not by a
  model's power or speed, but by the hybrid survivability of the human operator
  and the machine as a single system: its harmlessness in three circles — for the
  operator, for the people around while it works, and for the people affected by
  the outcome. First generation extends human capabilities; second generation
  extends and protects. Companion to the essay "The Second Generation of AI".
  Written with the participation of AI (Claude, ChatGPT).
keywords:
